From: Cosmopod OS Build Team <builds@cosmopod.invalid>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 00:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fdtput: mark create_node input mutable

create_node deliberately splits the supplied argv string in place.  Its
parameter therefore cannot be const.  Correct the declaration so newer glibc
strrchr declarations do not expose an invalid qualifier conversion.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 fdtput.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fdtput.c b/fdtput.c
index 80c2dcf..efac2c9 100644
--- a/fdtput.c
+++ b/fdtput.c
@@ -227,7 +227,7 @@ static int encode_value(struct display_info *disp, char **arg, int arg_count,
  * @param node_name	Name of node to create
  * @return new node offset if found, or -1 on failure
  */
-static int create_node(char **blob, const char *node_name)
+static int create_node(char **blob, char *node_name)
 {
 	int node = 0;
 	char *p;
-- 
2.43.0
